          "argument": "DEPTH",
          "detail": "Positive C int, with base-autodetected decimal, 0x hexadecimal or leading-zero octal spelling. Zero and negatives are rejected by this option's 'p' parser; the upper bound is the build's INT_MAX. A depth of N permits up to N intermediate CAs, plus leaf and trust anchor. Reference scope: OpenSSL 3.0.16.",
          "flag": "-verify",
          "summary": "Set positive intermediate-CA depth; zero is invalid",
          "value_semantics": {
            "schema_version": 1,
            "variants": [
